<div class="editorial-home">
  <div class="editorial-column">
    <h1 id="_top">Build business software without rebuilding the foundation.</h1>

    <section class="editorial-section editorial-section--first" aria-labelledby="why-dygo">
      <h2 id="why-dygo">The Go framework for business software</h2>
      <div class="editorial-prose">
        <p>Define your data and business logic. dygo provides PostgreSQL schema sync, permissions, background jobs, APIs, and Studio: a shared interface for working with your Records.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section" aria-labelledby="model">
      <h2 id="model">Define the business</h2>
      <div class="editorial-prose">
        <p><strong>Apps</strong> group your business modules. <strong>Entities</strong> define their data in YAML. <strong>Go</strong> handles Hooks and Jobs. <strong>Studio</strong> turns that metadata into forms, lists, and Record details.</p>
        <p>Shared conventions give developers and coding agents a consistent structure to build on.</p>
      </div>
      <p><a href="/start-here/core-concepts/">Explore the core concepts →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section" aria-labelledby="foundation">
      <h2 id="foundation">Built in</h2>
      <ul class="editorial-list">
        <li><span>›</span> PostgreSQL schema sync and explicit database Patches</li>
        <li><span>›</span> Authentication, roles, and Entity permissions</li>
        <li><span>›</span> Record APIs and transactional Hooks</li>
        <li><span>›</span> Durable Jobs, retries, and Schedules</li>
        <li><span>›</span> Encrypted secrets, Activity history, and diagnostic Logs</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section" aria-labelledby="loop">
      <h2 id="loop">Start a project</h2>
      <p>With dygo installed and PostgreSQL running:</p>
      <ol class="editorial-commands" aria-label="dygo quickstart commands">
        <li><span>›</span><code>dygo new my-system</code></li>
        <li><span>›</span><code>cd my-system</code></li>
        <li><span>›</span><code>dygo db prepare</code></li>
        <li><span>›</span><code>dygo setup</code></li>
        <li><span>›</span><code>dygo dev</code></li>
      </ol>
      <p><a href="/start-here/quickstart/">Follow the quickstart →</a></p>
    </section>

    <section class="editorial-section" aria-labelledby="current">
      <h2 id="current">Early development. Source available.</h2>
      <p>APIs and file formats can change before the first stable release. dygo uses the O'Saasy License.</p>
      <p><a href="/reference/status/">Check framework status →</a></p>
    </section>

